      "text": "There are nine teams, so we need to find the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9. This is given by the binomial coefficient $\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9 \\cdot 8}{2} = 36$.\n\nEach team plays three games with each of the other teams, so each of these 36 pairs of teams plays 3 games.\n\nThe total number of games played is the product of the number of pairs of teams and the number of games each pair plays, which is $36 \\cdot 3 = \\boxed{108}$.The answer is: 108",
